+# Circuit Debugger Contract
+
+## `simulate(gates, inputs)`
+
+### Behaviors
+1. Returns all wire values (inputs + computed) after propagating through gates
+2. AND gate: output 1 iff both inputs are 1
+3. OR gate: output 1 if at least one input is 1
+4. XOR gate: output 1 if exactly one input is 1
+5. Handles dependency chains (gate B depends on gate A's output)
+6. Works with the 4-bit adder example: 5 + 3 = 8
+7. Handles all inputs being 0
+8. Handles all inputs being 1
+
+### Verification
+- Unit tests for each gate type
+- Chain dependency test
+- Full adder correctness test
+
+## `findSwappedWires(gates)`
+
+### Behaviors
+1. Identifies all 8 wires involved in 4 output-wire swaps
+2. Returns sorted array of wire names
+3. Handles swaps of z-wire with internal wire
+4. Handles swaps of partial-sum wire with another wire
+5. Handles swaps of generate/propagate wire with another wire  
+6. Handles swaps of carry wire with another wire
+7. Works for circuits with up to 45 input bits (~220 gates) in < 5 seconds
+8. Correctly traces ripple-carry adder structure bit by bit
+
+### Verification
+- Test with known swaps on generated adder circuits
+- Test with different swap types (z-swap, partial-swap, carry-swap)
+- Performance test with 45-bit adder
